// InfoBadge: A small badge that draws attention to an item (WinUI's `InfoBadge`): a dot, an
// icon or a number. A [`value`](Self::value) of 0 or more is shown as a number and takes
// precedence over the [`icon_source`](Self::icon_source); with the value -1 (the default) the
// badge shows the icon of its icon source, and a dot without one. The control sets the states
// of WinUI as pseudo-classes, which the control theme of the WinUI theme
// (`src/FerroUI.Themes.WinUI/Controls/InfoBadge.xaml`) styles: `:dot`, `:icon`, `:font-icon`
// (an icon of a [`FontIconSource`]) and `:value` (DisplayKindStates). The template binds the
// number to [`value`](Self::value) and the icon and the corner radius to the
// [`template_settings`](Self::template_settings). The Fluent and Simple themes have no
// template for it (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 5.1). Differences from WinUI
// (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 10.2): a value below -1 is coerced to -1 and
// logged, where WinUI throws; whether `CornerRadius` is local is followed from the priority of
// its changes.
