// NavigationView: A navigation pane with menu items and a content area (WinUI's
// `NavigationView`). The pane is at the left (`Left`, `LeftCompact`, `LeftMinimal`, or chosen
// by the width in `Auto`: the display modes `Expanded`, `Compact` and `Minimal`) or at the top
// (`Top`). The template of the WinUI theme is WinUI's (`NavigationView.xaml`): the control
// finds WinUI's parts (`RootSplitView`, `TogglePaneButton`, `NavigationViewBackButton`,
// `NavigationViewCloseButton`, `PaneAutoSuggestButton`, `PaneTitleTextBlock`,
// `PaneTitleHolder`, `PaneTitlePresenter`, `PaneTitleOnTopPane`, `MenuItemsHost`,
// `FooterMenuItemsHost`, `TopNavMenuItemsHost`, `TopFooterMenuItemsHost`, the content controls
// of the pane header, custom content, footer and auto suggest box of the left and the top
// pane, `ContentLeftPadding`), sets their contents and the values of
// [`template_settings`](Self::template_settings) as WinUI's code does, and sets WinUI's visual
// states as pseudo-classes (`:compact`, `:expanded`, `:minimal`, `:top-navigation-minimal`,
// `:minimal-with-back-button`, `:toggle-pane-button-visible`, `:header-collapsed`,
// `:auto-suggest-box-collapsed`, `:closed-compact`, `:list-size-compact`,
// `:pane-not-overlaying`, `:back-button-collapsed`, `:pane-collapsed`, and
// `:back-button-row-visible` for the row WinUI sizes in code). The Fluent and Simple themes
// have no template. The menu items are realized in stack panels, not in `ItemsRepeater`s with
// a hierarchical `SelectionModel` (follow-up F1). Missing (docs/porting/winui-controls.md,
// section 10.4): the overflow of the top pane, the animations of the pane, the shadow of the
// pane, the padding of the title bar, the shoulder navigation and the selectors of templates
// and styles.
type NavigationView struct{ ContentControl }

