// PagerControl: A control to move through the pages of a paged content (WinUI's
// `PagerControl`): buttons to the first, previous, next and last page around a combo box of
// the page numbers, a number box to type one, or a button for each page (`DisplayMode`).
// `NumberOfPages` is -1 while the number of pages is not known; `SelectedPageIndex` is the
// index of the page, from 0, kept in the range of the pages, and its changes raise
// `SelectedIndexChanged`. The template is the control theme of the WinUI theme
// (`Controls/PagerControl.xaml`, from WinUI's `PagerControl.xaml`), with WinUI's parts
// `FirstPageButton`, `PreviousPageButton`, `NextPageButton`, `LastPageButton`,
// `ComboBoxDisplay`, `NumberBoxDisplay`, `NumberPanelItemsRepeater` and
// `NumberPanelCurrentPageIndicator`. The control sets WinUI's visual states as pseudo-classes:
// `:numberbox`, `:combobox` and `:numberpanel` (the display mode), `:infinite`
// (InfiniteItems), and for each button `:<button>collapsed`, `:<button>hidden` and
// `:<button>disabled` (`:firstcollapsed`, `:nexthidden`, ...). The Fluent and Simple themes
// have no template for it (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, section 5.1). Differences
// (docs/porting/winui-controls.md, G2): the number panel is an items control whose panel is a
// horizontal stack panel, where WinUI has an `ItemsRepeater` with a `StackLayout`
// (`ferroui-controls` cannot depend on the repeater crate); the indicator of the current page
// moves without WinUI's `RepositionThemeTransition`.
