// XamlLight: A light of the object model (WinUI `Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Media.XamlLight`). A
// subclass gives the light an id ([`get_id`](XamlLightImpl::get_id)) and creates its
// composition light when the light is connected to the element that holds it
// ([`on_connected`](XamlLightImpl::on_connected)), setting it with
// [`set_composition_light`](Self::set_composition_light). The light then lights, in the
// subtree of that element: - the elements that target its id
// ([`add_target_element`](Self::add_target_element)): their composition visuals are targets of
// the composition light, which lights their content; - the XAML brushes that target its id
// ([`add_target_brush`](Self::add_target_brush)): the scene lighting effects of those brushes
// receive the light. The composition light is in the coordinates of the element that holds it
// (its `CoordinateSpace` is the composition visual of that element).
type XamlLight struct{ Object }

